\title{A pricing rule that sends a limit a few ticks past the opposite touch}
\description{
The \code{marketable} pricing rule of a plan: a limit a few ticks past the other side of the book.

UBI reads the opposite touch when it sends the order, the best offer for a buy and the best bid for a sell, and sets the limit \code{buffer_ticks} past it, so the order trades at once like a market order but cannot fill far from the book. With no book to price against, or a quote marked stale, the order waits for the next tick, even an order sent only when a fill arrives, such as a hedge.
}
